- journal_page "Connect a Dreamwidth journal"
- described_by = ("connection-problem" if @problem)

.card
  .card__header
    %h1 Connect a Dreamwidth journal
  - if @problem
    = render "journal/connections/problem", problem: @problem, connection: @connection, existing: @existing

  %p
    Connecting uses an API key from Dreamwidth. It lets Plural Profiles read and
    post to that one journal. The key is stored encrypted, and is never shown
    in full again after you save it. Your Dreamwidth password never comes here.

  %ol.connect-steps
    %li Log in to Dreamwidth as the account you want to connect.
    %li
      %strong= link_to "Get your key from Dreamwidth (opens in a new tab)", "https://www.dreamwidth.org/api/getkey", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener"
    %li Copy the key that page shows, then come back to this tab and paste it below.

  = form_with model: @connection, scope: :connection, url: journal_connect_path, method: :post do |form|
    .form-group
      = form.label :username, "Dreamwidth username"
      = form.text_field :username, required: true, maxlength: 25,
        autocomplete: "off", autocapitalize: "none", spellcheck: false,
        aria: { describedby: described_by }, data: { "1p-ignore": "true" }
    .form-group
      = form.label :api_key, "API key"
      -# Always empty: a key is never shown back, and an empty field means the
      -# next paste can't get mixed up with the last one.
      = form.text_field :api_key, value: "", required: true,
        autocomplete: "off", autocapitalize: "none", spellcheck: false,
        aria: { describedby: ["api-key-hint", described_by].compact.join(" ") }, data: { "1p-ignore": "true" }
      %p.form-hint#api-key-hint
        You can revoke it any time in
        = dreamwidth_link_to("https://www.dreamwidth.org/manage/settings/?cat=mobile") { "Dreamwidth's mobile settings" }
        and it stops working here at once.
    .form-group.journal-actions
      = form.submit "Connect"
      = link_to "Back to your journals", journal_root_path, class: "btn btn--secondary"
